      "content": "Welcome to NebulaFlow, the automated deployment engine at GridScale designed to accelerate container orchestration and ensure consistent, repeatable infrastructure rollout across all environments. Automated deployment is critical for reducing manual errors and enabling rapid iteration, allowing our teams to focus on code quality rather than infrastructure setup. Before proceeding, ensure you have the NebulaFlow CLI installed locally, an active GridScale account, and a valid API token that possesses read permissions for the target cluster region.\n\nTo authenticate your local environment, run the `nf auth login` command followed by your assigned token string; this step establishes a secure session required for all subsequent infrastructure operations. Once authenticated, initialize your first production cluster by executing the `nf cluster init` command, specifying `--region us-east-1` to select your data center and `--size small` to allocate the minimum viable node pool for developmental testing. Before deploying your application, review your `production.yaml` configuration file to confirm that the specified container images exist and that the resource limits align with your environment's quota constraints.\n\nExecute the `nf deploy` command with the path to your configuration file to trigger the sequence of container image pulls, node scaling events, and rollout checks necessary for a stable launch. The CLI will",
